Nothing else in the shipped package is third-party code. There are no bundled
fonts (the panel uses the operating system's UI font stack), no icon sets, no
frameworks, and no dependencies installed at build time that reach the customer:
the only entry in package.json's devDependencies, acorn, is used by the ES3
checker and is never packaged.

Build-time tools the publisher uses, which are not distributed with the product
and so are not licensed to the customer:

  - acorn (MIT) — parses host scripts in scripts/check-es3.js.
  - ZXPSignCmd (Adobe) — signs the .zxp. Downloaded at release time by
    .github/workflows/release.yml, pinned to a commit and verified by SHA-256.
    Not part of the product.
